Technical Design & Architecture

1. Overview

This document describes the internal architecture, design decisions, and execution flow of the Most Active Cookie Analyzer CLI tool. It explains how the system processes log files, computes cookie frequencies, and returns the most active cookie(s) for a given UTC date.

2. High‑Level Architecture

Core Components

CLI Layer — Parses flags (-f, -d), validates input, and triggers execution.

Analyzer Engine — Reads the CSV file, filters entries by date, counts frequencies, and returns the result.

Integration Tests — Validate end‑to‑end behavior across CLI + analyzer.

