3. Data Flow

 3.1. CLI parses flags

Validates file path

Validates date format (YYYY-MM-DD)

3.2 Analyzer opens CSV file

Uses buffered streaming to avoid loading entire file

3.3 Each row is processed

Parse cookie + timestamp

Convert timestamp → UTC date

If date matches target:

Increment frequency counter

3.4 After file scan

Determine max frequency

Collect all cookies with that frequency

3.5 Return results

CLI prints each cookie on a new line

4. Key Design Decisions

4.1 Streaming File Processing

Avoids loading entire CSV into memory

Supports very large log files

Uses bufio.Scanner for efficient line-by-line reading

4.2 UTC Date Normalization

All timestamps converted to UTC

Ensures correctness across time zones

Uses time.Parse(time.RFC3339)

4.3 Frequency Map

map[string]int used for O(1) increments

Single pass through file → O(n) complexity

4.4 Deterministic Output

Cookies printed in the order they appear in the log

No sorting required

Matches problem specification

